From fa13917b33333c63a5c974ca3789007ea7ff5878 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <services.claude@accounts.ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:38:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0242 -- keep one read-only handle per package
 across asset opens (opt-in)

Every packaged asset opens through File::OpenFile(filename, start, end), and
each open fopen()ed the package again: on DJGPP findfirst + open + IOCTL +
truename, and a close later -- two directory lookups per open. On the 486 a
first play's asset_open is a fixed ~55 ms (AUDH16), and this reopen is part
of it (docs/lab/io.md).

Why sharing one FILE is exact: BufferedStream never relies on where the base
FILE was left -- Open() seeks END then BEGIN, every refill seeks to its
absolute position first, a direct large read seeks to _position first -- so
section streams on one read-only FILE, interleaved or not, read the same
bytes they would from their own FILE; WrapHandle streams never fclose it.

Why retire instead of close on a library change: a stream opened earlier
(music streaming, say) may still read through the handle, and fclose under it
is the one way this could go wrong. A library change only retires the table
entry (later opens get a fresh handle); handles are closed at engine exit;
the table is bounded and falls back to the plain fopen when full.

Opt-in: DOSAGS_PAKHANDLE=1. The manifest reports "DOS-PORT pakhandle
opened= reused= fallback= closed=".
---
 Common/data/assetmanager.cpp |  6 ++++
 Common/util/file.cpp         | 68 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 Common/util/file.h           |  5 +++
 Engine/main/quit.cpp         |  7 ++++
 4 files changed, 86 insertions(+)

